WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:07.835
Outside, Scrooge walked along, greeting everyone on the streets with a delighted smile.

2
00:00:07.836 --> 00:00:11.997
A pair of men noticed his joy and smiled in return.

3
00:00:11.998 --> 00:00:19.348
"Good morning, sir!" one said, tipping his hat. "Merry Christmas to you."

4
00:00:19.349 --> 00:00:24.268
"Thank you, sir, and I wish you the same," Scrooge said.

5
00:00:24.269 --> 00:00:30.983
He hadn't gone much farther when he spotted one of the gentlemen who had visited his office the day before.

6
00:00:30.984 --> 00:00:34.218
It sent a pang through his heart now.

7
00:00:34.219 --> 00:00:41.135
Scrooge had sent him away, yelling horribly about putting poor people in prison.

8
00:00:41.136 --> 00:00:46.831
"My dear sir!" Scrooge hurried to catch up to the gentleman.

9
00:00:46.832 --> 00:00:50.878
"A merry Christmas to you!"

10
00:00:50.879 --> 00:00:56.280
"Mr. Scrooge?" the gentleman said in surprise.

11
00:00:56.281 --> 00:00:59.837
"That's my name," Scrooge said.

12
00:00:59.838 --> 00:01:03.402
"Though I fear you may not think much of it.

13
00:01:03.403 --> 00:01:08.991
Still, I hope a generous donation to the poor will change your mind."

14
00:01:08.992 --> 00:01:14.069
He whispered an amount of money into the man's ear.

15
00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:16.625
The man's eyes went wide.

16
00:01:16.626 --> 00:01:25.445
"Mr. Scrooge, are you serious? You want to donate all that money?"

17
00:01:25.446 --> 00:01:29.222
"I am serious," Scrooge said.

18
00:01:29.223 --> 00:01:30.813
"Not a penny less.

19
00:01:30.814 --> 00:01:37.558
Will you please do me the favor of accepting it, and seeing that it helps the poor?"

20
00:01:37.559 --> 00:01:41.833
"I will, of course! Thank you!"

21
00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:46.588
Scrooge nodded. "Come to see me at my office tomorrow.

22
00:01:46.589 --> 00:01:49.903
I'll give you the money then."

23
00:01:49.904 --> 00:01:57.659
Scrooge continued on his way, patting children on the head and giving coins to beggars.

24
00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:04.280
"What a wonderful, beautiful holiday!" he thought.

25
00:02:04.281 --> 00:02:07.965
Finally he reached his nephew's house.

26
00:02:07.966 --> 00:02:14.539
He wanted to stop and knock but his knees trembled.

27
00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:22.429
He had to pass by the door a dozen times before he finally found the courage to knock.

28
00:02:22.430 --> 00:02:25.929
A servant brought him to the dining room.

29
00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:34.461
Scrooge peered nervously into the room filled with Fred and his family, as well as some guests.

30
00:02:34.462 --> 00:02:40.239
"Why, bless my soul! Who's that?" Fred said.

31
00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:45.711
"I've . . . I've . . ." Scrooge's voice quaked.

32
00:02:45.712 --> 00:02:52.084
"I've, um, come to dinner. Will you let me in, Fred?"

33
00:02:52.085 --> 00:02:59.672
"Of course!" Fred took his uncle's hand and nearly shook Scrooge's arm off.

34
00:02:59.673 --> 00:03:04.576
The family immediately made Scrooge feel at home.

35
00:03:04.577 --> 00:03:09.050
He was welcomed by Fred's wife and by their children.

36
00:03:09.051 --> 00:03:12.404
Other guests chatted politely with him.

37
00:03:12.405 --> 00:03:18.241
It was a wonderful party, with delicious food and entertaining games.

38
00:03:18.242 --> 00:03:25.646
Scrooge stayed late and enjoyed himself thoroughly.

39
00:03:25.647 --> 00:03:30.916
Even so, he was up early the next morning to go to work.

40
00:03:30.917 --> 00:03:35.663
In fact, he arrived even earlier than usual.

41
00:03:35.664 --> 00:03:39.436
"Good," he thought as he sat at his desk.

42
00:03:39.437 --> 00:03:45.834
"Cratchit isn't here yet. I hope he comes in late this morning."

43
00:03:45.835 --> 00:03:52.899
And so he did. Cratchit was a full 18 minutes late when he finally arrived.

44
00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:59.589
He rushed in, leaping onto his stool as if he were trying to catch up with the clock.

45
00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:06.825
"What do you mean by showing up here at this time of day?" Scrooge growled.

46
00:04:06.826 --> 00:04:13.275
"I'm sorry, sir," Cratchit said meekly. "I . . . My family and I . . ."

47
00:04:13.276 --> 00:04:16.424
"Step this way!"

48
00:04:16.425 --> 00:04:21.525
Cratchit cowered as he followed his boss across the room.

49
00:04:21.526 --> 00:04:26.507
"It's only once a year, sir. It won't happen again."

50
00:04:26.508 --> 00:04:33.585
"Well, the current way of doing things around here is unacceptable," Scrooge snapped.

51
00:04:33.586 --> 00:04:40.553
"And therefore . . ." He couldn't stop a smile from taking the place of his angry scowl.

52
00:04:40.554 --> 00:04:46.441
"I'm going to raise your salary! Merry Christmas, Bob!"

53
00:04:46.442 --> 00:04:53.271
Cratchit gazed at him in amazement. "Are you serious, Mr. Scrooge?"

54
00:04:53.272 --> 00:04:56.251
Scrooge clapped him on the back.

55
00:04:56.252 --> 00:05:00.674
"I haven't given you a very merry Christmas for many years now.

56
00:05:00.675 --> 00:05:04.021
But I wish to make up for that.

57
00:05:04.022 --> 00:05:09.074
I'll raise your salary, and do whatever I can to help your family.

58
00:05:09.075 --> 00:05:13.889
That includes hiring the best doctors for Tiny Tim."

59
00:05:13.890 --> 00:05:22.799
"But . . . But . . ." Tears filled Cratchit's eyes. "Thank you, sir."

60
00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:32.143
"Don't thank me, Bob. Please go home to your family and take another day off!"

61
00:05:32.144 --> 00:05:35.178
Scrooge was as good as his word.

62
00:05:35.179 --> 00:05:44.144
Thanks to the doctors he hired, the tragic scene shown by the Ghost of Christmas Future never appeared.

63
00:05:44.145 --> 00:05:47.784
Instead Tiny Tim thrived.

64
00:05:47.785 --> 00:05:54.211
Not only that, but he also grew up thinking of Ebenezer Scrooge as a second father.

65
00:05:54.212 --> 00:05:59.020
And Scrooge didn't stop there, with the Cratchit family.

66
00:05:59.021 --> 00:06:03.534
Instead he became a charitable man.

67
00:06:03.535 --> 00:06:08.569
Everyone who knew him observed the same thing.

68
00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:15.785
He kept the kind and loving spirit of Christmas with him all year long.

69
00:06:15.786 --> 00:06:22.999
"That's what I strive for every day of my life," he said to anyone who asked him about it.

70
00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:28.707
"May that be said of all of us—that we are kind and loving.

71
00:06:28.708 --> 00:06:38.297
As Tiny Tim might say, God bless us, everyone!"

